Third-party attribution

Sift contains no third-party code and has no package dependencies. Two projects
informed its design, and both are acknowledged here with thanks.

uninstally — https://github.com/gostonx/uninstally
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Codenta.
The leftover-discovery strategy in
Sources/AppAudit/Services/LeftoverScanner.swift is adapted from uninstally.
Attribution is preserved in that source file. Its MIT terms are compatible
with the licence above.

Mole — https://github.com/tw93/Mole
GNU General Public License v3.0, Copyright (c) tw93.
Mole is the reason Sift shows a running-app indicator and offers a sort by
last-used date, and it was studied for its protection-list and Homebrew-path
concepts. No Mole source is present in Sift: Mole is written in Go, Sift in
Swift, and these behaviours are independent implementations against Apple's
own APIs (NSRunningApplication and Spotlight's kMDItemLastUsedDate). What was
taken is the idea, which carries no licence obligation; Mole remains
separately licensed under the GPL-3.0 and no part of it is redistributed
here.
